1
00:00:10,967 --> 00:00:12,621
RIGHT. AGENTS?

2
00:00:12,621 --> 00:00:15,450
MA'AM.AGENT HIGHTOWER.

3
00:00:15,450 --> 00:00:17,800
YEAH. ALL RIGHT. NARCOTICS
NEEDS HELP GETTING INTEL

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,889
ON A METH HOUSE
IN THE SOUTHWEST.

5
00:00:19,889 --> 00:00:22,848
I SAID I COULD SPARE
TWO OF YOU.SURE. WE'LL GET IT.

6
00:00:22,848 --> 00:00:24,415
VAN PELT AND CHO.

7
00:00:27,288 --> 00:00:28,898
WHAT'S THE JOB?

8
00:00:39,517 --> 00:00:42,912
[liquid drips]

9
00:00:47,308 --> 00:00:51,312
IT'S HARD TO BELIEVE
THERE'S INTEL IN THESE.THERE BETTER BE.
IT'S DRIPPING ON MY FEET.

10
00:00:51,312 --> 00:00:54,228
HIGHTOWER KNOWS ABOUT
RIGSBY AND ME.NOTICED THAT.

11
00:00:54,228 --> 00:00:57,231
SHE KNOWS,
BUT SHE HASN'T SAID ANYTHING.

12
00:00:57,231 --> 00:00:59,233
WHY DO YOU THINK THAT IS?NO IDEA.

13
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:01,191
IF YOU COULD GUESS.I WOULDN'T.

14
00:01:01,191 --> 00:01:03,193
[sighs]

15
00:01:03,193 --> 00:01:05,587
I CAN'T STOP
THINKING ABOUT IT.

16
00:01:05,587 --> 00:01:08,590
[engine starts]THAT'S JUST GONNA GET YOU
IN TROUBLE.

17
00:01:11,114 --> 00:01:14,335
CAN YOU HELP ME?
CAN YOU HELP ME?

18
00:01:14,335 --> 00:01:15,945
WHAT HAPPENED TO YOU?

19
00:01:15,945 --> 00:01:18,513
I LOST MY SHOE.

20
00:01:18,513 --> 00:01:21,472
CAN YOU TELL ME WHERE I AM?I'M--I'M GONNA CALL THIS IN,
ALL RIGHT?

21
00:01:21,472 --> 00:01:22,995
MA'AM. MA'AM.

22
00:01:22,995 --> 00:01:24,345
CAN YOU...

23
00:01:24,345 --> 00:01:26,260
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

24
00:01:26,260 --> 00:01:29,263
WE'RE GONNA GET YOU
SOME MEDICAL ATTENTION. COME ON.OKAY.

25
00:01:29,263 --> 00:01:31,352
COME OVER HERE AND SIT DOWN.OKAY.

26
00:01:31,352 --> 00:01:32,962
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

27
00:01:32,962 --> 00:01:35,095
MM.

28
00:01:35,095 --> 00:01:36,357
MA'AM?

29
00:01:36,357 --> 00:01:37,575
MA'AM?

30
00:01:37,575 --> 00:01:39,229
GRACE.

31
00:01:39,229 --> 00:01:41,840
HEY. SHE SAID
SHE CAN'T REMEMBER WHO SHE IS,

32
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,060
WHERE SHE CAME FROM
OR WHAT HAPPENED.

33
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:46,236
NO I.D.
NOTHING ON HER AT ALL.

34
00:01:46,236 --> 00:01:48,064
WHERE'S LISBON?SHE'S ON HER WAY.

35
00:01:48,064 --> 00:01:51,067
E.M.T.s THINK THE BULLET
GRAZED THE VICTIM'S HEAD.

36
00:01:51,067 --> 00:01:53,069
I THOUGHT
WE SHOULD TALK TO HER HERE.

37
00:01:53,069 --> 00:01:55,680
SHE LOST HER SHOE, SO SHE
COULDN'T HAVE WALKED FAR.

38
00:01:55,680 --> 00:01:58,640
THE CRIME SCENE'S
PROBABLY NEARBY.GOOD THINKING.

39
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:01,556
[police radio chatter]SO SHOULD WE WAIT FOR LISBON
OR...

40
00:02:01,556 --> 00:02:03,210
NAH. HI.

41
00:02:03,210 --> 00:02:06,691
I'M PATRICK JANE.
HOW YOU DOING?

42
00:02:06,691 --> 00:02:09,390
[panting] MY HEAD HURTS.

43
00:02:09,390 --> 00:02:12,871
I DON'T REMEMBER WHO I AM.

44
00:02:12,871 --> 00:02:14,830
[exhales deeply]

45
00:02:17,049 --> 00:02:18,529
HOLD MY HAND.

46
00:02:18,529 --> 00:02:21,619
I'M GONNA TRY
AND HELP WITH THE PAIN.

47
00:02:21,619 --> 00:02:23,621
OKAY,
I WANT YOU TO CONCENTRATE

48
00:02:23,621 --> 00:02:26,015
AND LET THE PAIN FLOW
OUT THROUGH YOUR ARM

49
00:02:26,015 --> 00:02:27,669
AND INTO MY HAND.

50
00:02:27,669 --> 00:02:31,890
JUST LET IT FLOW,
LIKE WATER.

51
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:33,892
AH, I CAN FEEL IT.

52
00:02:33,892 --> 00:02:35,503
CAN YOU FEEL THAT?

53
00:02:35,503 --> 00:02:36,678
YES.

54
00:02:36,678 --> 00:02:38,680
CAN YOU FEEL IT FLOWING?YEAH.

55
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:42,031
THE PAIN IS FLOWING AWAY.

56
00:02:44,120 --> 00:02:46,383
TELL ME YOUR NAME.

57
00:02:46,383 --> 00:02:48,385
DON'T REACH.

58
00:02:48,385 --> 00:02:51,301
JUST WAIT FOR IT.

59
00:02:51,301 --> 00:02:52,781
I CAN'T.

60
00:02:52,781 --> 00:02:54,174
AH, THAT'S OKAY.

61
00:02:54,174 --> 00:02:57,264
THAT'S OKAY.

62
00:02:57,264 --> 00:03:00,136
WHAT WERE YOU DOING THIS
MORNING, BEFORE YOU GOT HURT?

63
00:03:00,136 --> 00:03:01,790
[whispers] I CAN'T.

64
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:04,096
IT'S OKAY. DON'T WORRY.[sniffles]

65
00:03:04,096 --> 00:03:08,362
TONIGHT, THEN, BEFORE MY FRIENDS
FOUND YOU, WHAT WERE YOU DOING?

66
00:03:08,362 --> 00:03:10,581
I-I WAS IN A ROOM.

67
00:03:10,581 --> 00:03:12,496
IT'S COLD.

68
00:03:12,496 --> 00:03:15,238
CAN YOU SEE ANYTHING?

69
00:03:17,327 --> 00:03:19,895
IT'S--IT'S TOO DARK.

70
00:03:19,895 --> 00:03:23,159
WERE YOU SITTING IN A CHAIR
OR WERE YOU LYING DOWN?

71
00:03:23,159 --> 00:03:26,249
LYING DOWN.ON THE FLOOR OR ON THE BED?

72
00:03:26,249 --> 00:03:27,859
ON THE FLOOR.

73
00:03:27,859 --> 00:03:30,122
THERE'S...

74
00:03:30,122 --> 00:03:33,517
DIRT AND STRAW.

75
00:03:33,517 --> 00:03:35,737
[clears throat]

76
00:03:35,737 --> 00:03:39,088
IT MAKES ME COUGH.

77
00:03:39,088 --> 00:03:42,091
WHAT DOES IT SMELL LIKE?HORSES.

78
00:03:42,091 --> 00:03:44,180
THAT'S FANTASTIC.

79
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:45,573
GRACE?

80
00:03:45,573 --> 00:03:47,618
YEAH. WE'RE LOOKING
FOR A STABLE.

81
00:03:47,618 --> 00:03:48,924
YEAH.

82
00:03:48,924 --> 00:03:51,013
[Patrick clears throat]

83
00:03:58,499 --> 00:04:01,893
HER SHOE.

84
00:04:06,594 --> 00:04:10,162
YEAH, THAT'S HER SHOE.

85
00:04:10,162 --> 00:04:13,035
[Patrick] OKAY.

86
00:04:15,167 --> 00:04:17,257
[Patrick clears throat]

87
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:19,694
OKAY.

88
00:04:21,609 --> 00:04:23,350
[Patrick] ALL RIGHT.

89
00:04:26,048 --> 00:04:28,398
[whispers] GUYS, THERE'S
A LIGHT SWITCH RIGHT HERE.

90
00:04:28,398 --> 00:04:29,356
[click]

91
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:35,057
OH.

92
00:04:35,057 --> 00:04:37,015
UH-OH.

93
00:04:53,380 --> 00:04:55,947
THE BULLET CREASED HER SKULL.
IT DIDN'T FRACTURE THE BONE,

94
00:04:55,947 --> 00:04:58,863
BUT A HIT LIKE THAT CAN KNOCK
YOU AROUND SOMETHING WICKED.

95
00:04:58,863 --> 00:05:00,865
SHE COULD HAVE BEEN UNCONSCIOUS
FOR A WHILE.

96
00:05:00,865 --> 00:05:02,911
SHOOTER PROBABLY THOUGHT
SHE WAS DEAD

97
00:05:02,911 --> 00:05:06,088
AND DUMPED HER
WITH THE OTHER BODIES.WHAT ABOUT THE AMNESIA?

98
00:05:06,088 --> 00:05:08,090
I DON'T KNOW WHAT TO TELL YOU.

99
00:05:08,090 --> 00:05:10,092
RETROGRADE AMNESIA
USUALLY RECEDES WITH TIME,

100
00:05:10,092 --> 00:05:12,137
BUT I DON'T KNOW HOW FAST
THAT'LL HAPPEN.

101
00:05:12,137 --> 00:05:15,227
OKAY, WHAT I WANT YOU TO DO IS
JUST FOCUS ON THE QUEEN.

102
00:05:15,227 --> 00:05:18,274
HERE'S THE LADY.
NOW YOU SAW WHERE SHE IS.

103
00:05:18,274 --> 00:05:20,668
THERE'S THE LADY.

104
00:05:20,668 --> 00:05:21,930
OKAY. NOW TELL ME...

105
00:05:23,888 --> 00:05:25,673
WHERE'S THE QUEEN?

106
00:05:25,673 --> 00:05:28,110
WRONG.
FIRST BOY YOU EVER KISSED.

107
00:05:28,110 --> 00:05:30,547
I DON'T KNOW.

108
00:05:30,547 --> 00:05:33,637
WHAT'S YOUR FIRST NAME?I DON'T KNOW. I'M SORRY.

109
00:05:33,637 --> 00:05:35,770
LOOK, THERE SHE WAS.
SHE WAS ALWAYS THERE.

110
00:05:35,770 --> 00:05:38,381
RIGHT IN THE MIDDLE.AND THE POINT BEING?

111
00:05:38,381 --> 00:05:40,427
OH, I'M JUST MAKING SURE
SHE HAS AMNESIA,

112
00:05:40,427 --> 00:05:42,472
WHICH, BY THE WAY, YOU DO.

113
00:05:42,472 --> 00:05:45,519
IT'S HARD TO LIE WHEN YOU'RE
THINKING ABOUT SOMETHING ELSE.

114
00:05:45,519 --> 00:05:49,871
[whispers] GREAT.WE'RE CHECKING
OUR MISSING PERSONS DATABASE,

115
00:05:49,871 --> 00:05:52,700
THEN WE'LL RUN YOUR PRINTS.
SOMETHING'LL PROBABLY COME UP.[cell phone rings]

116
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:55,920
FIND SOMEBODY TO COME IN
AND PRINT HER.OKAY.

117
00:05:55,920 --> 00:05:58,836
AGENT HIGHTOWER.MORNING, LISBON.
AS SOON AS IT'S PRACTICAL,

118
00:05:58,836 --> 00:06:01,404
I WANT TO SEE YOU, VAN PELT
AND RIGSBY IN MY OFFICE.

119
00:06:01,404 --> 00:06:04,233
I'VE BEEN MEANING TO ADDRESS
THIS ISSUE FOR A WHILE,

120
00:06:04,233 --> 00:06:06,453
BUT THERE'S BEEN SO MUCH
COMING ACROSS MY DESK,

121
00:06:06,453 --> 00:06:08,890
I HAVEN'T HAD THE TIME.

122
00:06:08,890 --> 00:06:11,936
FIRST OFF,
NEITHER OF YOU IS DENYING

123
00:06:11,936 --> 00:06:14,069
YOU'RE IN
A SEXUAL RELATIONSHIP?

124
00:06:14,069 --> 00:06:16,332
ARE YOU?NO.

125
00:06:16,332 --> 00:06:18,856
NO, MA'AM.YOU WORK TOGETHER,
YOU DEVELOP FEELINGS.

126
00:06:18,856 --> 00:06:20,554
NOTHING WRONG WITH THAT.

127
00:06:20,554 --> 00:06:22,730
BUT YOU KNOW VERY WELL
IT'S AGAINST CBI RULES,

128
00:06:22,730 --> 00:06:24,862
AND LIKE I TELL MY KIDS,
RULES ARE RULES.

129
00:06:24,862 --> 00:06:28,431
IF YOU WANT TO STAY TOGETHER,
THAT'S YOUR CHOICE.

130
00:06:28,431 --> 00:06:30,955
BUT ONE OF YOU HAS TO TRANSFER
OUT OF THE UNIT.

131
00:06:30,955 --> 00:06:33,567
IF YOU BOTH WANT
TO STAY IN THE UNIT,

132
00:06:33,567 --> 00:06:35,569
THEN YOU CAN'T BE TOGETHER.

133
00:06:35,569 --> 00:06:37,222
THAT'S WHAT IT IS.

134
00:06:37,222 --> 00:06:39,747
GIVE ME YOUR DECISION
TOMORROW AT THE LATEST.

135
00:06:43,490 --> 00:06:44,882
QUESTIONS?

136
00:06:44,882 --> 00:06:46,493
NO, MA'AM.NO.

137
00:06:46,493 --> 00:06:47,537
OKAY.

138
00:06:50,932 --> 00:06:53,848
LISBON, STAY A MOMENT.

139
00:06:53,848 --> 00:06:56,894
WHY DIDN'T YOU HANDLE
THIS SITUATION YOURSELF?

140
00:06:56,894 --> 00:06:58,983
I WON'T DEFEND
WHAT I DID, MA'AM--

141
00:06:58,983 --> 00:07:00,985
I UNDERSTAND THESE TWO
SNEAKING AROUND,

142
00:07:00,985 --> 00:07:02,770
BUT YOU'RE THEIR SUPERIOR.

143
00:07:02,770 --> 00:07:05,686
I EXPECT MORE.

144
00:07:05,686 --> 00:07:07,209
[sighs]

145
00:07:07,209 --> 00:07:09,994
I'LL BE WRITING
A CORRECTIVE MEMO.

146
00:07:09,994 --> 00:07:11,474
THAT'S IT.

147
00:07:11,474 --> 00:07:13,389
THANK YOU FOR YOUR TIME.

148
00:07:21,441 --> 00:07:23,443
I DON'T WANT TO TALK ABOUT IT.

149
00:07:24,879 --> 00:07:28,404
CHO, WHERE ARE WE
WITH THE VICTIMS?

150
00:07:28,404 --> 00:07:31,189
I VERIFIED THE TWO I.D.s
WE FOUND AT THE SCENE.

151
00:07:31,189 --> 00:07:33,017
JANINE AND MITCHELL LANGHAM
FROM CHICO,

152
00:07:33,017 --> 00:07:36,151
BOTH IN THEIR 50s,
NO FAMILY IN STATE.

153
00:07:36,151 --> 00:07:39,154
NEIGHBOR SAID THAT THEY WERE
HIKING IN KASTEN STATE FOREST.THAT'S 100 MILES
FROM WHERE WE FOUND THEM.

154
00:07:39,154 --> 00:07:42,462
WELL, WHAT ABOUT
THE THIRD VICTIM?SAME AS THE JANE DOE.
NO I.D. OF ANY KIND.

155
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:44,942
THE CORONER SAYS
HE'S IN HIS EARLY 20s.

156
00:07:44,942 --> 00:07:49,164
I PUT HIS PRINTS
INTO THE SYSTEM.VAN PELT, DID YOU GET
ANY HITS ON THEM? VAN PELT?

157
00:07:49,164 --> 00:07:52,428
UH, I'LL CHECK. I'LL CHECK.THE CORONER THINKS
THAT THEY WERE SHOT

158
00:07:52,428 --> 00:07:54,822
WITH A HIGH-POWERED RIFLE--
THE LANGHAMS UP CLOSE,

159
00:07:54,822 --> 00:07:56,606
OUR JANE DOE
AND THE UNIDENTIFIED MALE

160
00:07:56,606 --> 00:07:59,696
FROM A DISTANCE.DO EITHER OF THE LANGHAMS
HAVE A RECORD?

161
00:07:59,696 --> 00:08:02,786
NO.I THINK WE CAN SET
THE LANGHAMS ASIDE.

162
00:08:02,786 --> 00:08:05,528
I THINK THEY WERE BY-PRODUCTS.
WEREN'T PLANNED.OH?

163
00:08:05,528 --> 00:08:07,878
YEAH. THE FIRST TWO VICTIMS
WERE SHOT FROM A DISTANCE,

164
00:08:07,878 --> 00:08:09,532
I.D.s WERE TAKEN.

165
00:08:09,532 --> 00:08:12,666
TWO VICTIMS WERE SHOT UP-CLOSE.
I.D.s WERE NOT TAKEN.

166
00:08:12,666 --> 00:08:15,756
CLEARLY, THE FIRST TWO VICTIMS
WERE THE TARGETS.AND WHEN THE LANGHAMS
ROLL UP TO THE SCENE,

167
00:08:15,756 --> 00:08:17,584
WRONG PLACE, WRONG TIME.

168
00:08:17,584 --> 00:08:20,108
KILLER SHOOTS THE LANGHAMS,
FREAKS OUT.

169
00:08:20,108 --> 00:08:22,110
DOESN'T BOTHER
TO TAKE THEIR I.D.s.

170
00:08:22,110 --> 00:08:23,938
DOESN'T EVEN NOTICE

171
00:08:23,938 --> 00:08:26,897
THAT ONE OF THE FIRST VICTIMS
THAT HE SHOT WAS ONLY WOUNDED.

172
00:08:26,897 --> 00:08:28,986
WE GOT A HIT
ON THE MALE VICTIM'S PRINTS.

173
00:08:28,986 --> 00:08:30,640
HIS NAME'S LEONARD RAILTON,

174
00:08:30,640 --> 00:08:33,338
NATIVE AMERICAN, LIVED ON
THE STORM RIVER RESERVATION.

175
00:08:33,338 --> 00:08:35,297
THAT'S RIGHT NEXT
TO THE STATE FOREST.

176
00:08:35,297 --> 00:08:37,386
OH, HE'S BEEN IN AND OUT
OF THE SYSTEM

177
00:08:37,386 --> 00:08:39,519
SINCE HIS EARLY TEENS--
MOSTLY SMALL STUFF,

178
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:41,259
A COUPLE OF DRUG BUSTS.

179
00:08:41,259 --> 00:08:43,697
NO FAMILY LISTED. HIS EMERGENCY
CONTACT IS HIS PAROLE OFFICER.

180
00:08:43,697 --> 00:08:45,786
GO AND GO SHOW JANE DOE
A PICTURE OF LEONARD

181
00:08:45,786 --> 00:08:48,963
AND THE LANGHAMS.
IT'S WORTH A SHOT.OKAY.

182
00:08:48,963 --> 00:08:52,575
YOU GUYS CHECK OUT THE TRAIL
THAT THE LANGHAMS WERE HIKING.

183
00:08:52,575 --> 00:08:55,491
IT SOUNDS LIKE
SOMETHING'S GOING ON UP THERE.

184
00:08:55,491 --> 00:08:57,798
LET'S GO TALK
TO RAILTON'S P.O.[lowered voice] HEY.

185
00:08:57,798 --> 00:09:00,496
THERE'S NO POINT IN HIDING
YOUR FRUSTRATION WITH HIGHTOWER.

186
00:09:00,496 --> 00:09:02,542
I MEAN, SOONER OR LATER,

187
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:04,761
YOU'RE JUST GONNA EXPLODE
WITH SUPPRESSED RAGE.

188
00:09:04,761 --> 00:09:07,068
WITH ANY LUCK,
YOU'LL BE NEXT TO ME.

189
00:09:07,068 --> 00:09:09,723
WELL, THAT'S WHAT
I'M WORRIED ABOUT.

190
00:09:09,723 --> 00:09:11,246
GRACE.

191
00:09:11,246 --> 00:09:12,682
YOU OKAY?

192
00:09:12,682 --> 00:09:14,423
SURE. [sighs]

193
00:09:14,423 --> 00:09:15,729
NO. YOU?

194
00:09:15,729 --> 00:09:18,209
THIS IS A GOOD THING, OKAY?

195
00:09:18,209 --> 00:09:21,822
NO MORE SNEAKING AROUND. WE GET
TO DECIDE WHAT WE WANNA DO.DO WE KNOW WHAT THAT IS?

196
00:09:21,822 --> 00:09:24,433
LET'S JUST GET THROUGH THE DAY,
AND THEN TONIGHT,

197
00:09:24,433 --> 00:09:28,480
WE'LL OPEN UP A BOTTLE OF WINE
AND WE'LL TALK, OKAY?YEAH. SOUNDS GOOD.

198
00:09:28,480 --> 00:09:30,961
[whispers] I LOVE YOU.[whispers] I LOVE YOU.

199
00:09:33,181 --> 00:09:37,185
[woman] I THOUGHT LEONARD
HAD A CHANCE, YOU KNOW?

200
00:09:37,185 --> 00:09:40,841
GOOD KID. REALLY TRYING
NOT TO REPEAT OLD MISTAKES.

201
00:09:40,841 --> 00:09:43,713
HOW LONG WERE YOU LEONARD'S
PAROLE OFFICER, MS. BRINTON?

202
00:09:43,713 --> 00:09:45,889
A LITTLE OVER A YEAR.

203
00:09:45,889 --> 00:09:48,805
HE HAVE ANY FAMILY
WE SHOULD SPEAK TO?

204
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:50,851
NO, LEONARD DIDN'T HAVE
ANYBODY.

205
00:09:50,851 --> 00:09:53,854
BUT HIS MOTHER WAS SHOSHONE,
GREW UP ON THE RESERVATION.

206
00:09:53,854 --> 00:09:56,726
THAT'S WHY I GOT HIM TO MOVE
THERE AFTER HE WAS RELEASED.WHY THE RESERVATION?

207
00:09:56,726 --> 00:09:59,729
LEONARD NEEDED PEOPLE
IN HIS LIFE WHO CARED ABOUT HIM.

208
00:09:59,729 --> 00:10:02,384
HE COULD GET THAT THERE.
IT'S A SMALL COMMUNITY--

209
00:10:02,384 --> 00:10:05,474
NOT TOO WELL-OFF, BUT TIGHT.DO YOU LIVE THERE?

210
00:10:05,474 --> 00:10:07,476
MM-HMM. MY FATHER'S CLAN IS
FROM THERE. I'M SHOSHONE.

211
00:10:07,476 --> 00:10:09,086
SHOSHONE, UH,

212
00:10:09,086 --> 00:10:11,785
WITH A NEW YORK ITALIAN/IRISH
THING GOING ON,

213
00:10:11,785 --> 00:10:14,178
IF I'M NOT MISTAKEN
BY THE ACCENT.

214
00:10:14,178 --> 00:10:16,180
IS THAT
FROM YOUR MOTHER'S SIDE?

215
00:10:16,180 --> 00:10:18,792
I'M NOT THE FIRST PERSON
WHO NEEDED TIME

216
00:10:18,792 --> 00:10:20,750
TO FIGURE OUT WHO SHE WAS.MM.

217
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:22,665
WERE THERE ANY INDICATIONS

218
00:10:22,665 --> 00:10:24,667
THAT LEONARD WAS DOING
ANYTHING ILLEGAL?

219
00:10:24,667 --> 00:10:27,844
NO. HE HAD SOME PROBLEMS
WHEN HE FIRST GOT THERE,

220
00:10:27,844 --> 00:10:30,847
BUT ABOUT SIX MONTHS AGO,
HE SETTLED DOWN, GOT A JOB,

221
00:10:30,847 --> 00:10:34,721
HAD A GIRLFRIEND
IN THE VALLEY.WHAT WAS HER NAME?

222
00:10:34,721 --> 00:10:37,071
DERRIEN HOPWOOD.
I MET HER A COUPLE OF TIMES.

223
00:10:37,071 --> 00:10:38,681
NO RECORD.

224
00:10:38,681 --> 00:10:40,596
GOOD INFLUENCE,
I THOUGHT.

225
00:10:40,596 --> 00:10:41,815
IS THIS HER?

226
00:10:43,773 --> 00:10:46,776
UH... NO,
I DON'T KNOW THIS WOMAN.

227
00:10:46,776 --> 00:10:48,952
POSITIVE?I SAID NO.

228
00:10:48,952 --> 00:10:50,345
I GOT IT.

229
00:10:52,086 --> 00:10:54,828
DOES LEONARD HAVE ANY FRIENDS
ON THE RESERVATION

230
00:10:54,828 --> 00:10:56,830
WE SHOULD TALK TO?YOU'RE GOING ON THE REZ?

231
00:10:56,830 --> 00:11:00,703
YEAH.WILL THE TRIBAL POLICE BE
WITH YOU?

232
00:11:00,703 --> 00:11:02,531
OH, THEY'RE AWARE
OF THE INVESTIGATION.

233
00:11:02,531 --> 00:11:06,361
WE'LL KEEP THEM IN THE LOOP.I SHOULD GO WITH YOU.

234
00:11:06,361 --> 00:11:07,754
OH, THAT'S NOT NECESSARY.

235
00:11:07,754 --> 00:11:10,321
AS FAR AS SOME OF THEM
ARE CONCERNED,

236
00:11:10,321 --> 00:11:12,323
YOU'RE FOREIGNERS--
FOREIGNERS WITH BADGES.

237
00:11:12,323 --> 00:11:13,673
YOU WON'T GET ANYTHING.

238
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,762
I'LL GET MY COAT.

239
00:11:15,762 --> 00:11:19,287
EXCELLENT. WELL,
WE GOT OURSELVES A NATIVE GUIDE.

240
00:11:19,287 --> 00:11:21,506
YES.

241
00:11:21,506 --> 00:11:23,813
[Rigsby]
JANINE AND MITCHELL LANGHAM.

242
00:11:23,813 --> 00:11:26,555
RING ANY BELLS?[sighs] NO,
BUT I DON'T REALLY MEET PEOPLE

243
00:11:26,555 --> 00:11:29,558
UNLESS THEY'RE IN TROUBLE.WELL, THESE PEOPLE GOT
INTO TROUBLE.

244
00:11:29,558 --> 00:11:31,995
BEEN ANY REPORTS
OF CRIME ON THE TRAILS?

245
00:11:31,995 --> 00:11:34,955
ROBBERIES, ASSAULTS?NO, JUST, YOU KNOW, RACCOONS,
BIRDS, DEER, RATTLESNAKES, BEAR.

246
00:11:34,955 --> 00:11:37,871
WELL, I DON'T THINK
A BEAR SHOT FOUR PEOPLE

247
00:11:37,871 --> 00:11:39,916
WITH A HIGH-POWERED RIFLE.NO, BEARS CAN'T DO THAT.

248
00:11:39,916 --> 00:11:42,136
THEIR NEIGHBOR SAID
THE LANGHAMS WOULD'VE WALKED

249
00:11:42,136 --> 00:11:45,139
THE MORNINGSTAR TRAIL.HUH. MORNINGSTAR IS NOT
ONE OF OUR MORE POPULAR TRAILS.

250
00:11:45,139 --> 00:11:48,316
[indistinct radio chatter]EXCUSE ME. I GOT--UH...
UH, TISDALE, STAND BY ONE.

251
00:11:48,316 --> 00:11:50,927
LOOK, I GOTTA GO.
I GOTTA GO UP THE HILL THERE.

252
00:11:50,927 --> 00:11:52,929
WE HAVE
AN ANIMAL CONTROL ISSUE.

253
00:11:52,929 --> 00:11:55,932
WELL, WE NEED TO CHECK OUT
THAT TRAIL.[sighs] OKAY, UH...

254
00:11:55,932 --> 00:11:58,108
OKAY, THE TRAILHEAD
IS RIGHT OVER THERE.

255
00:11:58,108 --> 00:12:00,154
YOU JUST STAY ON THE PATH.

256
00:12:00,154 --> 00:12:03,113
WHEN YOU GET TO THE FORK,
YOU GO TO THE LEFT, OKAY?

257
00:12:03,113 --> 00:12:05,637
JUST STAY TO THE LEFT.
YOU'LL BE FINE.

258
00:12:05,637 --> 00:12:07,117
GOT IT. LEFT. THANKS.

259
00:12:07,117 --> 00:12:09,641
[woman] I DON'T RECOGNIZE
ANY OF THEM.

260
00:12:11,121 --> 00:12:13,950
TAKE YOUR TIME.
THINK ABOUT IT.

261
00:12:13,950 --> 00:12:17,258
I HAVE. THESE PEOPLE ARE
ALL DEAD, RIGHT?

262
00:12:17,258 --> 00:12:18,738
YES.

263
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:21,044
THERE'S ONE PIECE
OF GOOD NEWS.

264
00:12:21,044 --> 00:12:23,612
WE RAN YOU THROUGH
THE FINGERPRINTS DATABASE.

265
00:12:23,612 --> 00:12:25,092
YOU'RE NOT THERE.

266
00:12:25,092 --> 00:12:27,311
HOW IS THAT GOOD NEWS?

267
00:12:27,311 --> 00:12:29,313
IT MEANS
YOU'RE NOT A CRIMINAL...

268
00:12:29,313 --> 00:12:32,142
ORYOU'RE
A VERY, VERY GOOD ONE.

269
00:12:32,142 --> 00:12:33,753
[chuckles]

270
00:12:37,887 --> 00:12:41,543
HOW'S IT GOING
WITH THE, UM...

271
00:12:41,543 --> 00:12:44,720
MISSING PERSONS THING?

272
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:47,201
WELL, NO ONE'S FILED
A MISSING PERSONS REPORT

273
00:12:47,201 --> 00:12:48,724
FITTING YOUR DESCRIPTION
YET,

274
00:12:48,724 --> 00:12:51,771
BUT I'M SURE
IT'S JUST A MATTER OF TIME.

275
00:12:51,771 --> 00:12:53,773
YOU DON'T KNOW THAT.

276
00:12:53,773 --> 00:12:56,732
LOOK, YOU HAD A JOB TO DO,
AND YOU DID IT. THANKS.

277
00:12:56,732 --> 00:12:58,821
YOU DON'T HAVE TO STAY.

278
00:12:58,821 --> 00:13:00,736
I'LL STICK AROUND.

279
00:13:03,086 --> 00:13:06,089
[voice breaking] OKAY.

280
00:13:06,089 --> 00:13:08,048
THANKS.

281
00:13:08,048 --> 00:13:10,311
I'VE GOT A LOT OF TIME
INVESTED HERE,

282
00:13:10,311 --> 00:13:13,270
BUT IF SHE LEAVES, WE'RE INTO
THIS WHOLE SEXISM THING

283
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:15,316
OF WHOSE JOB IS
MORE IMPORTANT.

284
00:13:15,316 --> 00:13:17,753
LIKE I SAID,
IT'S COMPLICATED.NO, IT ISN'T.

285
00:13:17,753 --> 00:13:20,800
WHAT?WHICH DO YOU WANT MORE--
YOUR JOB OR VAN PELT?

286
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:23,541
WHAT? IT--IT'S NOT THAT EASY.SURE IT IS.
THIS IS THE FORK, RIGHT?

287
00:13:23,541 --> 00:13:27,067
NO, WE--WE TOOK THE FORK.NO, I DON'T THINK
THAT WAS THE FORK.

288
00:13:27,067 --> 00:13:30,026
I THINK THIS IS THE FORK.WELL, WHATEVER. GO LEFT.

289
00:13:30,026 --> 00:13:31,680
IT'S NOT THAT SIMPLE.

290
00:13:31,680 --> 00:13:34,204
JOB OR VAN PELT.
ALL THERE IS TO IT.

291
00:13:45,476 --> 00:13:47,827
[Brinton] THE REC CENTER'S
THE COMMUNITY GATHERING SPOT.

292
00:13:47,827 --> 00:13:49,741
LEONARD USED TO COME HERE.

293
00:13:53,833 --> 00:13:55,486
THIS IS JOSEPH SILVERWING.

294
00:13:55,486 --> 00:13:58,098
HE HELPED
TO SETTLE LEONARD IN HERE.

295
00:13:58,098 --> 00:14:00,361
HE'S ON THE TRIBAL COUNCIL.

296
00:14:00,361 --> 00:14:02,842
JOSEPH, THESE ARE THE DETECTIVES
FROM CBI I CALLED YOU ABOUT.TERESA LISBON. HI.

297
00:14:02,842 --> 00:14:04,539
PATRICK JANE.

298
00:14:04,539 --> 00:14:06,933
WE'RE INVESTIGATING THE MURDER
OF LEONARD RAILTON.

299
00:14:06,933 --> 00:14:08,935
CAN YOU TELL US ANYTHING
ABOUT HIM?

300
00:14:08,935 --> 00:14:12,068
HE'S A GOOD KID. WORKED HARD.
STAYED OUT OF TROUBLE.

301
00:14:12,068 --> 00:14:14,723
WE HEARD HE HAD A JOB.

302
00:14:14,723 --> 00:14:16,986
DOWN AT, UH,
MARKHAM WILLIS'S PLACE.

303
00:14:16,986 --> 00:14:19,075
IT'S A SOUVENIR SHOP
JUST OFF THE RESERVATION.

304
00:14:19,075 --> 00:14:21,077
WAS LEONARD HAVING
ANY PROBLEMS?

305
00:14:21,077 --> 00:14:22,818
NO.

306
00:14:22,818 --> 00:14:25,734
DID YOU HEAR ABOUT
ANY ARGUMENTS OR FIGHTS?

307
00:14:25,734 --> 00:14:27,127
NO.

308
00:14:27,127 --> 00:14:29,216
MONEY PROBLEMS?
HEALTH ISSUES?

309
00:14:29,216 --> 00:14:30,913
NO.

310
00:14:30,913 --> 00:14:33,742
YOU'RE RIGHT. YOU REALLY ARE
OPENING THINGS UP HERE.

311
00:14:33,742 --> 00:14:35,744
DO YOU KNOW ABOUT
ANY RELATIONSHIPS

312
00:14:35,744 --> 00:14:38,355
HE WAS HAVING
OFF THE RESERVATION MAYBE?NO.

313
00:14:38,355 --> 00:14:41,793
[indistinct conversations]

314
00:14:45,797 --> 00:14:47,321
NICE SHOT.

315
00:14:49,192 --> 00:14:51,760
DID YOU GUYS KNOW
LEONARD RAILTON?

316
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:53,936
[tap, balls clatter]

317
00:14:53,936 --> 00:14:56,069
I'LL TAKE THAT AS A YES.

318
00:14:56,069 --> 00:14:58,723
I'M TRYING TO FIND
THE PERSON WHO KILLED HIM.

319
00:14:58,723 --> 00:15:01,683
DO YOU WANT TO HELP ME
WITH THAT?

320
00:15:01,683 --> 00:15:03,946
DON'T ALL SPEAK AT ONCE.

321
00:15:03,946 --> 00:15:05,817
WHO'S GONNA TALK FIRST?

322
00:15:05,817 --> 00:15:07,907
[chuckles]
WE DON'T TALK TO PO-PO.

323
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,996
PO-PO?

324
00:15:09,996 --> 00:15:11,649
I LIKE THAT.

325
00:15:11,649 --> 00:15:15,262
BUT I'M NOT PO-PO.
I'M A PO-PO CONSULTANT.

326
00:15:15,262 --> 00:15:17,699
HOW ABOUT THIS?

327
00:15:17,699 --> 00:15:22,008
I BET THAT I CAN SINK A BALL
BEFORE YOUR BEST PLAYER CAN,

328
00:15:22,008 --> 00:15:25,707
AND HE CAN HAVE
THREE CHANCES TO MY ONE,

329
00:15:25,707 --> 00:15:30,364
AND IF I LOSE...
50 BUCKS. HUH?

330
00:15:30,364 --> 00:15:34,150
BUT IF I WIN,
YOU TELL ME ABOUT LEONARD.

331
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,457
WE GOT A DEAL?

332
00:15:36,457 --> 00:15:38,285
GREAT.
WHO'S YOUR SHARPSHOOTER?

333
00:15:38,285 --> 00:15:40,940
IT'S YOU, ISN'T IT, SHORTY?
LET'S DO THIS.

334
00:15:40,940 --> 00:15:42,593
OKAY.

335
00:15:42,593 --> 00:15:44,552
ALL RIGHT.
FIRST BALL IN WINS.

336
00:15:44,552 --> 00:15:45,988
[balls clatter]

337
00:15:45,988 --> 00:15:48,338
YOU GET THREE CHANCES.
I GET ONE.

338
00:15:48,338 --> 00:15:49,992
OKAY.

339
00:15:49,992 --> 00:15:52,255
AND BY THE WAY,
THAT GIRL YOU'RE CRUSHING ON,

340
00:15:52,255 --> 00:15:55,128
THE ONE IN THE BLUE SWEATER--
IT'S NEVER GONNA HAPPEN.

341
00:15:55,128 --> 00:15:57,826
SHE'S INTO THE TALL GUY.
GOOD LUCK.

342
00:15:57,826 --> 00:15:59,741
MY MONEY'S ON THE KID.

343
00:16:02,657 --> 00:16:04,964
[Patrick] ONE.

344
00:16:06,704 --> 00:16:09,272
TWO.

345
00:16:09,272 --> 00:16:12,710
LAST TIME. GOOD LUCK.
LUCKY LAST.

346
00:16:12,710 --> 00:16:14,930
THAT'S THREE.

347
00:16:14,930 --> 00:16:18,107
THERE'S A HOLE
IN THAT BALL.[ball clatters]

348
00:16:18,107 --> 00:16:20,370
HERE'S THE HARD PART.

349
00:16:20,370 --> 00:16:22,068
[groans]

350
00:16:27,073 --> 00:16:29,292
[Patrick groans]

351
00:16:30,990 --> 00:16:33,209
OOH! SCHOOLED YA.

352
00:16:35,472 --> 00:16:37,735
OKAY, SO, UH,
WHAT WAS LEONARD'S STORY?

353
00:16:37,735 --> 00:16:41,696
HE HAD MONEY.
A LOT OF IT.

354
00:16:41,696 --> 00:16:43,654
ALWAYS HAD
THE NEWEST KICKS.

355
00:16:43,654 --> 00:16:45,743
SINCE WHEN?

356
00:16:45,743 --> 00:16:47,093
LIKE, SIX MONTHS AGO.

357
00:16:47,093 --> 00:16:49,747
WELL, I HEARD
HE HAD A JOB.

358
00:16:49,747 --> 00:16:52,707
[scoffs] OH, YEAH.
AT WILLIS'S SOUVENIR SHOP?

359
00:16:52,707 --> 00:16:55,057
THAT'S PENNIES.

360
00:16:55,057 --> 00:16:56,667
LEONARD HAD MONEY.

361
00:16:56,667 --> 00:16:59,888
ANY IDEA WHERE THAT
MIGHT HAVE COME FROM?

362
00:16:59,888 --> 00:17:01,542
HE WOULDN'T SAY.

363
00:17:01,542 --> 00:17:04,501
BUT HE WAS OUT IN THE WOODS
ALL THE TIME,

364
00:17:04,501 --> 00:17:06,068
SO... WE FIGURED,
YOU KNOW?

365
00:17:06,068 --> 00:17:07,765
YES?

366
00:17:07,765 --> 00:17:10,029
[chuckles] EVERYBODY KNOWS
WHAT GOES ON IN THE WOODS.

367
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:12,031
[chuckles] OH, SURE.
THE WOODS.

368
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,989
YEAH,
THIS IS NOT THE TRAIL.

369
00:17:13,989 --> 00:17:15,643
IT'S OVER HERE.

370
00:17:15,643 --> 00:17:18,515
ARE YOU SURE? I THOUGHT
I SAW IT OVER HERE.

371
00:17:20,082 --> 00:17:22,606
WATER TANK?

372
00:17:24,869 --> 00:17:26,958
[Rigsby] CHO?

373
00:17:26,958 --> 00:17:28,960
YEAH?

374
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:32,181
THERE'S A POT PLANT HERE.

375
00:17:32,181 --> 00:17:34,705
ACTUALLY, THERE'S A WHOLE BUNCH
OF POT PLANTS HERE.

376
00:17:34,705 --> 00:17:37,360
IT LOOKS LIKE A FARM.OH, YEAH,

377
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:39,754
WHICH MEANS THERE'S PROBABLY
SOME BAD GUYS WITH GUNS.

378
00:17:39,754 --> 00:17:43,584
[gunshots]

379
00:17:43,584 --> 00:17:45,368
[pants]

380
00:17:45,368 --> 00:17:48,023
[pants] NO BARS.
SO MUCH FOR BACKUP.

381
00:17:50,330 --> 00:17:52,767
[gunshots]

382
00:17:52,767 --> 00:17:54,986
[panting]THERE'S ONLY ONE SHOOTER.
YOU DRAW FIRE,

383
00:17:54,986 --> 00:17:57,641
AND I'LL TAKE HIM FROM THE SIDE.
READY? ONE... TWO...ONE... TWO...

384
00:17:57,641 --> 00:17:59,208
THREE!GO.

385
00:18:15,006 --> 00:18:16,399
RIGSBY! CLEAR!

386
00:18:16,399 --> 00:18:18,923
GOT IT!

387
00:18:18,923 --> 00:18:22,927
[both panting]

388
00:18:28,890 --> 00:18:32,894
IT'S THE KIND OF FARM YOU FIND
ALL OVER PUBLIC LANDS--

389
00:18:32,894 --> 00:18:36,202
ABOUT AN ACRE OF PLANTS,
IRRIGATION PIPES EVERYWHERE.[Cho] MUST BE TAPPING
INTO WATER FROM UP THE VALLEY.

390
00:18:36,202 --> 00:18:38,856
DID YOU HIT THE SHOOTER?
MAYBE HE'S IN A HOSPITAL.DIDN'T SEE ANY BLOOD.
I DOUBT IT.

391
00:18:38,856 --> 00:18:41,511
DO YOU THINK THE RANGER
KNOWINGLY DIRECTED YOU

392
00:18:41,511 --> 00:18:44,471
TOWARD THE POT FARM?
WAS THIS A SETUP?IT'S HARD TO SAY.
WE GOT PRETTY TURNED AROUND.

393
00:18:44,471 --> 00:18:47,648
I'M NOT EXACTLY SURE
WE WERE ON THE TRAIL.WHERE'S THE RANGER NOW?

394
00:18:47,648 --> 00:18:50,999
UP IN THE MOUNTAINS. SUPERVISOR
SAYS HE'S OUT OF CALLING RANGE.FIND OUT WHEN HE'S BACK.

395
00:18:50,999 --> 00:18:53,871
SO IT LOOKS LIKE LEONARD RAILTON
WAS WORKING FOR THE POT FARMERS.

396
00:18:53,871 --> 00:18:58,049
THERE'S A HUNDRED WAYS
THAT COULD TURN UGLY.MEH. IF LEONARD WAS FARMIN'
THE WEED,

397
00:18:58,049 --> 00:19:00,922
HE WOULD'VE TOLD HIS FRIENDS
ABOUT IT.

398
00:19:00,922 --> 00:19:04,143
WHATEVER HE WAS DOING,
HE FELT SHAME OR AMBIVALENCE.

399
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:06,101
WHICH TAKES
THE INVESTIGATION WHERE?

400
00:19:06,101 --> 00:19:09,452
WELL, WE HAVEN'T SPOKEN
TO THE GIRLFRIEND YET.

401
00:19:09,452 --> 00:19:11,802
SO GO DO THAT.
YOU TWO TALK TO NARCOTICS.

402
00:19:11,802 --> 00:19:15,197
SEE IF THERE'S A LINE ON
MARIJUANA PLAYERS IN THAT AREA.

403
00:19:15,197 --> 00:19:18,418
YOU HEARD WHAT SHE SAID.

404
00:19:18,418 --> 00:19:21,725
WE WEREN'T LIVING TOGETHER
OR ANYTHING, JUST HANGING OUT.

405
00:19:21,725 --> 00:19:24,641
SO LEONARD ISN'T
THE BABY'S FATHER, MS. HOPWOOD?

406
00:19:24,641 --> 00:19:26,861
KAI'S FATHER?
[laughs] NO.

407
00:19:26,861 --> 00:19:28,036
[Kai fusses]

408
00:19:28,036 --> 00:19:30,430
OH, YEAH. I KNOW, HONEY.

409
00:19:30,430 --> 00:19:32,954
BUT LEONARD LIKED
YOUR LITTLE BOY, DIDN'T HE?

410
00:19:32,954 --> 00:19:35,739
SURE. [chuckles]

411
00:19:35,739 --> 00:19:38,916
LEONARD BOUGHT
MOST OF THE TOYS HERE.AND THIS, UH...

412
00:19:38,916 --> 00:19:42,268
ENORMOUS STACK
OF INFANT FORMULA.

413
00:19:42,268 --> 00:19:44,879
YEAH, LIKE,
1,000 BUCKS WORTH.

414
00:19:44,879 --> 00:19:46,228
[Kai fusses]

415
00:19:46,228 --> 00:19:48,230
WHAT'S THE STORY
WITH THAT?

416
00:19:48,230 --> 00:19:51,015
WELL, IT'S BECAUSE KAI GOT
THIS RASH.

417
00:19:51,015 --> 00:19:54,323
IT WAS GOING AROUND, YOU KNOW?
A COUPLE OF KIDS HAD IT.

418
00:19:54,323 --> 00:19:56,847
HE HAD THIS IDEA
IT WAS THE POWDERED FORMULA.

419
00:19:56,847 --> 00:19:59,285
HE MADE ME THROW
ALL THE POWDERED OUT,

420
00:19:59,285 --> 00:20:02,244
WHICH IS CRAZY,
'CAUSE IT'S CHEAPER,

421
00:20:02,244 --> 00:20:04,507
AND IT'S REAL EASY TO USE.

422
00:20:04,507 --> 00:20:07,467
ALL YOU DO IS ADD WATER.
[chuckles]

423
00:20:07,467 --> 00:20:10,600
HOW'S THE RASH NOW?

424
00:20:10,600 --> 00:20:12,254
[fusses]ALL GONE.

425
00:20:12,254 --> 00:20:14,038
[chuckles]

426
00:20:14,038 --> 00:20:16,911
I GUESS HE WAS RIGHT.

427
00:20:16,911 --> 00:20:19,609
YOU WEREN'T SURPRISED TO HEAR
ABOUT LEONARD, WERE YOU?

428
00:20:19,609 --> 00:20:21,655
I MEAN,
YOU--YOU CARED FOR HIM,

429
00:20:21,655 --> 00:20:24,614
BUT YOU WEREN'T STARTLED
TO LEARN THAT HE WAS DEAD.

430
00:20:24,614 --> 00:20:27,704
HE HAD MONEY,

431
00:20:27,704 --> 00:20:30,664
AND NOT FROM
THAT LAME SOUVENIR STORE JOB.

432
00:20:30,664 --> 00:20:33,884
HE WOULDN'T TELL ME
WHERE HE WAS GETTIN' IT.

433
00:20:33,884 --> 00:20:36,844
MY EXPERIENCE IS,
THAT MEANS TROUBLE.

434
00:20:36,844 --> 00:20:39,890
YOUR BEST GUESS?

435
00:20:39,890 --> 00:20:42,023
WHATEVER ELSE
HE WAS DOING...

436
00:20:42,023 --> 00:20:43,677
[Kai fussing]

437
00:20:43,677 --> 00:20:46,897
HE--HE WAS ALWAYS GOOD
TO ME AND KAI.

438
00:20:46,897 --> 00:20:51,162
HE WAS A GOOD MAN.
YOU FIND WHO DID THIS.

439
00:20:51,162 --> 00:20:53,164
WE'LL DO EVERYTHING WE CAN.

440
00:20:53,164 --> 00:20:54,688
[makes popping sound]

441
00:20:54,688 --> 00:20:56,516
[gasping]

442
00:20:56,516 --> 00:20:58,082
[imitates baby gurgling]

443
00:21:02,130 --> 00:21:05,089
[Lisbon] MR. WILLIS, HOW LONG
WAS LEONARD WORKING HERE?[packages rustle]

444
00:21:05,089 --> 00:21:08,658
UH...
I GUESS ABOUT SIX MONTHS.

445
00:21:08,658 --> 00:21:11,966
I HIRED HIM ON DOLORES BRINTON'S
RECOMMENDATION.

446
00:21:11,966 --> 00:21:14,316
HE WAS A GREAT KID,
GOOD WORKER.

447
00:21:14,316 --> 00:21:17,276
OH, YEAH.
THAT'S WHAT I'M TALKING 'BOUT.

448
00:21:17,276 --> 00:21:18,886
PRETTY GREAT, HUH?

449
00:21:18,886 --> 00:21:20,496
THIS IS FANTASTIC.

450
00:21:20,496 --> 00:21:22,150
D-DO YOU DELIVER?

451
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:24,848
AS A MATTER OF FACT, WE DO.ALL RIGHT.

452
00:21:24,848 --> 00:21:27,808
JANE, PUT IT BACK.WHAT?

453
00:21:27,808 --> 00:21:29,897
YOU HEARD ME. NOW.OKAY.

454
00:21:29,897 --> 00:21:31,290
NOW!

455
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,030
ALL RIGHT.

456
00:21:33,030 --> 00:21:34,728
WE THINK THAT, UH,

457
00:21:34,728 --> 00:21:37,687
LEONARD WAS GETTING MONEY
FROM SOMEPLACE ELSE.

458
00:21:37,687 --> 00:21:40,864
ANY IDEA WHAT THAT WAS ABOUT?NO. HE NEVER SAID A WORD
ABOUT IT. WHAT WAS HE DOING?

459
00:21:40,864 --> 00:21:42,779
WE'RE STILL WORKING
ON THAT.

460
00:21:42,779 --> 00:21:45,173
I CAN GIVE YOU A DEAL
ON THAT BONNET.

461
00:21:45,173 --> 00:21:47,393
SPECIAL
LAW ENFORCEMENT DISCOUNT.

462
00:21:47,393 --> 00:21:49,003
[chuckles]
YOU'RE NOT SELF-CONSCIOUS

463
00:21:49,003 --> 00:21:51,092
ABOUT PEDDLING
YOUR OWN CULTURE, ARE YOU?

464
00:21:51,092 --> 00:21:53,703
[chuckles]
THIS IS NOT MY CULTURE.

465
00:21:53,703 --> 00:21:56,010
THIS WAR BONNET IS
FROM THE LAGUNA PEOPLE.

466
00:21:56,010 --> 00:21:57,490
MM.

467
00:21:57,490 --> 00:21:59,840
IT HAS NOTHING TO DO
WITH US SHOSHONE.

468
00:21:59,840 --> 00:22:03,060
IT'S KIND OF A PASTICHE,
REALLY.

469
00:22:03,060 --> 00:22:05,585
BUT THAT'S WHAT
YOU AMERICANS WANT TO BUY,

470
00:22:05,585 --> 00:22:08,849
SO THAT'S WHAT I SELL.THANK YOU FOR YOUR TIME,
MR. WILLIS. JANE?

471
00:22:10,807 --> 00:22:12,156
JANE!

472
00:22:12,156 --> 00:22:14,768
I'LL MEET YOU OUTSIDE.

473
00:22:17,248 --> 00:22:20,295
IS THERE SOME KIND OF SERVICE
FOR LEONARD?

474
00:22:20,295 --> 00:22:21,992
TOMORROW AFTERNOON,
I BELIEVE.

475
00:22:21,992 --> 00:22:23,472
AH.

476
00:22:23,472 --> 00:22:24,865
THAT'S SUCH A SHAME.

477
00:22:24,865 --> 00:22:26,475
I'M GONNA TAKE THAT.

478
00:22:26,475 --> 00:22:28,825
AND I LIKE THIS ONE, TOO.

479
00:22:28,825 --> 00:22:31,393
IT'S REALLY BEAUTIFUL.
SO THAT AS WELL,

480
00:22:31,393 --> 00:22:33,917
AND, UM...

481
00:22:33,917 --> 00:22:36,877
THIS THING. I'LL SEE
IF I CAN GET A TUNE OUT OF THAT.

482
00:22:36,877 --> 00:22:40,010
JUST LOVE THOSE FEATHERS.
YEAH.MM.

483
00:22:40,010 --> 00:22:41,969
[plays notes]

484
00:22:41,969 --> 00:22:44,014
GRACE, HI. IT'S JANE.

485
00:22:44,014 --> 00:22:47,148
HOW'S IT GOING WITH JANE DOE
THERE? SHE GET A CLUE YET?

486
00:22:47,148 --> 00:22:48,758
MM, DIDN'T THINK SO.

487
00:22:48,758 --> 00:22:51,239
YOU KNOW, BRING HER
DOWN TO THE OFFICE.

488
00:22:51,239 --> 00:22:54,895
I THINK WE'RE GONNA HAVE TO GET
A LITTLE MORE INTERVENTIONIST.

489
00:22:54,895 --> 00:22:56,984
[Patrick] OKAY.

490
00:22:56,984 --> 00:23:00,291
IF YOU START TO FEEL DIZZY
OR WOOZY OR--OR ANYTHING--

491
00:23:00,291 --> 00:23:03,686
GRACE, QUIT HOVERING.
ALL RIGHT? SHE'S FINE.

492
00:23:03,686 --> 00:23:05,949
I TOOK HER
OUT OF THE HOSPITAL, JANE.

493
00:23:05,949 --> 00:23:08,952
SHE'S MY RESPONSIBILITY.I GET THAT, BUT SHE'S FINE.
AREN'T YOU?

494
00:23:08,952 --> 00:23:10,606
WHAT ARE THESE?

495
00:23:10,606 --> 00:23:13,566
OH, THESE ARE PICTURES
OF WHERE YOU'RE FROM.

496
00:23:13,566 --> 00:23:15,916
I DON'T KNOW
WHERE I'M FROM.

497
00:23:15,916 --> 00:23:17,613
SURE YOU DO.

498
00:23:17,613 --> 00:23:19,920
I'LL LAY MONEY ON THE FACT
THAT YOU'RE A LOCAL.

499
00:23:19,920 --> 00:23:22,575
YOU HAVE ROOTS AROUND HERE.

500
00:23:22,575 --> 00:23:25,621
YOU VISITED PLACES LIKE THIS
AS A KID.

501
00:23:25,621 --> 00:23:28,972
ONE OF THESE PICTURES HERE
WILL MEAN SOMETHING TO YOU.

502
00:23:28,972 --> 00:23:30,974
I GET NOTHING FROM THAT.

503
00:23:30,974 --> 00:23:33,890
WHAT ABOUT THIS? HMM?

504
00:23:33,890 --> 00:23:35,892
GRACE, A MINUTE?

505
00:23:35,892 --> 00:23:37,764
OH, SURE.
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK.

506
00:23:37,764 --> 00:23:39,766
OKAY.

507
00:23:39,766 --> 00:23:40,897
THIS?

508
00:23:43,030 --> 00:23:44,858
MNH-MNH.

509
00:23:44,858 --> 00:23:46,860
JUST RELAX.
DON'T WORK SO HARD.

510
00:23:46,860 --> 00:23:48,296
LOOK AT THAT.

511
00:23:48,296 --> 00:23:49,950
HAVE YOU EVER SEEN

512
00:23:49,950 --> 00:23:52,996
A MORE BEAUTIFUL,
MORE PEACEFUL PLACE?

513
00:23:52,996 --> 00:23:56,217
IT WOULD BE COOL
IF I COULD JUST SAY THE WORD,

514
00:23:56,217 --> 00:23:58,437
AND YOU COULD BE
RIGHT THERE,

515
00:23:58,437 --> 00:24:02,310
LISTENING
TO THE BIRDS SING...

516
00:24:02,310 --> 00:24:05,835
[lowers voice] THE WIND RUSTLING
THROUGH THE TREES...

517
00:24:05,835 --> 00:24:10,536
THE WATER LAPPING
AGAINST THE SHORE.

518
00:24:10,536 --> 00:24:13,321
IF I COULD JUST SAY THE WORD.

519
00:24:15,497 --> 00:24:18,544
[telephone rings]

520
00:24:18,544 --> 00:24:21,764
[sighs]
WAYNE, THIS COULDN'T WAIT?

521
00:24:30,773 --> 00:24:33,341
THIS IS SO SIMPLE.

522
00:24:33,341 --> 00:24:35,561
I LOVE YOU...

523
00:24:35,561 --> 00:24:38,128
MORE THAN--MORE THAN THIS JOB,
MORE THAN ANYTHING.

524
00:24:38,128 --> 00:24:40,130
[sighs]
YOU GOT SHOT AT TODAY.

525
00:24:40,130 --> 00:24:42,785
YOU'RE PUMPED FULL
OF ADRENALINE.NO, NO.

526
00:24:42,785 --> 00:24:44,961
WELL, YES,
BUT THAT DOESN'T MATTER.

527
00:24:44,961 --> 00:24:46,963
[gulps]

528
00:24:46,963 --> 00:24:48,965
I KNOW WHAT I WANT TO DO.

529
00:24:48,965 --> 00:24:52,360
[inhales deeply]
I, UH...

530
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:55,450
I TALKED TO A GUY IN
THE SAN FRANCISCO OFFICE TODAY.

531
00:24:55,450 --> 00:24:57,800
THERE'S AN OPENING
IN THE MAJOR CRIMES UNIT.

532
00:24:57,800 --> 00:25:00,803
IT'S ONLY
AN HOUR AND A HALF AWAY.

533
00:25:00,803 --> 00:25:04,546
YOU MEAN IT?PLEASE, LET'S JUST DO THIS.

534
00:25:04,546 --> 00:25:06,896
I-I DON'T CARE
WHERE I WORK.

535
00:25:06,896 --> 00:25:09,290
I-I WANT YOU.

536
00:25:09,290 --> 00:25:11,292
YOU REALLY MEAN IT?

537
00:25:11,292 --> 00:25:13,729
[whispers] YES, YES.

538
00:25:24,131 --> 00:25:25,959
REALLY? NOW?

539
00:25:25,959 --> 00:25:28,875
RANGER TISDALE SHOULD BE OFF
THE MOUNTAIN IN AN HOUR, SO...

540
00:25:28,875 --> 00:25:31,442
HIS BANK RECORDS SAY
HE'S DEPOSITING 2 GRAND A MONTH

541
00:25:31,442 --> 00:25:33,793
OVER AND ABOVE HIS SALARY--
CASH.

542
00:25:33,793 --> 00:25:35,708
LET'S GO TALK TO HIM.

543
00:25:42,889 --> 00:25:44,673
TISDALE.

544
00:25:46,109 --> 00:25:48,721
I WAS GONNA CALL YOU.
I JUST HEARD.

545
00:25:48,721 --> 00:25:51,201
POT FARM.
DOESN'T THAT BEAT EVERYTHING?

546
00:25:51,201 --> 00:25:54,596
YEAH,
RIGHT IN YOUR OWN WOODS.YEAH. I'VE BEEN HIKING
THESE TRAILS FOR EIGHT YEARS.

547
00:25:54,596 --> 00:25:57,164
I HAD NO IDEA. I DON'T KNOW
WHERE YOU ENDED UP,

548
00:25:57,164 --> 00:26:00,167
BUT YOU MUST'VE GOTTEN
SERIOUSLY TURNED AROUND.

549
00:26:00,167 --> 00:26:02,169
THAT'S HARD TO BELIEVE

550
00:26:02,169 --> 00:26:04,998
WHEN THE POT FARMERS ARE
PAYING YOU $2,000 A MONTH.

551
00:26:04,998 --> 00:26:08,871
2 TH--I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.YOU'RE GONNA HAVE
TO COME WITH US.

552
00:26:08,871 --> 00:26:10,656
[thud]OH!

553
00:26:14,355 --> 00:26:16,749
[grunts][grunts]

554
00:26:16,749 --> 00:26:18,577
[both grunting]

555
00:26:21,536 --> 00:26:23,146
NICE WORK.

556
00:26:23,146 --> 00:26:25,584
[panting] FELT GOOD.
[chuckles]

557
00:26:27,455 --> 00:26:29,109
SEND YOU TO THE FARM?

558
00:26:29,109 --> 00:26:31,720
I WAS TRYING LIKE HELL
TO KEEP YOU AWAY FROM IT.

559
00:26:31,720 --> 00:26:34,244
ALL YOU HAD TO DO
WAS STAY ON THE TRAIL.

560
00:26:34,244 --> 00:26:37,465
IS THAT REALLY SO HARD?SO YOU WERE TAKING MONEY
FROM THE POT DEALERS

561
00:26:37,465 --> 00:26:40,207
TO PROTECT THEIR FARM,
RIGHT?[sighs] THEY WERE PAYING ME

562
00:26:40,207 --> 00:26:42,862
TO DIRECT TOURISTS AWAY
AND LET 'EM KNOW

563
00:26:42,862 --> 00:26:46,996
IF THERE WERE ANY LOCAL COPS
OR FEDS SNOOPING AROUND.

564
00:26:46,996 --> 00:26:49,912
OKAY, THESE PEOPLE WHO GOT
KILLED--I NEVER EVEN SAW THEM.

565
00:26:49,912 --> 00:26:52,872
I NEED THE NAMES
OF THE PEOPLE WHO PAID YOU.

566
00:26:52,872 --> 00:26:54,656
I CAN'T DO THAT.

567
00:26:54,656 --> 00:26:57,441
LOOK, THESE AREN'T HIPPIES

568
00:26:57,441 --> 00:26:59,443
GROWING WEED IN THE FOREST,
OKAY?

569
00:26:59,443 --> 00:27:01,358
THESE ARE
SERIOUS, SERIOUS MEN.

570
00:27:01,358 --> 00:27:04,057
IF THEY LEARN THAT
I GAVE UP THEIR NAMES,

571
00:27:04,057 --> 00:27:06,668
THEY'LL KILL ME.

572
00:27:06,668 --> 00:27:09,976
LOOK, THEY KNOW
YOU'VE BEEN ARRESTED.

573
00:27:09,976 --> 00:27:12,369
THEY THINK YOU'RE
GIVING THEM UP RIGHT NOW.

574
00:27:12,369 --> 00:27:14,981
NOW WITH THESE MEN WALKING
AROUND, YOU'RE IN DANGER.

575
00:27:14,981 --> 00:27:18,027
GIVE US THEIR NAMES,
AND WE'LL LOCK THEM UP.NO, I CAN'T.

576
00:27:18,027 --> 00:27:19,986
IT'S YOUR CALL.

577
00:27:19,986 --> 00:27:23,119
YOU GOT A FAMILY?UH, YEAH.

578
00:27:23,119 --> 00:27:25,339
WELL, I SUGGEST
YOU SEND THEM SOMEWHERE.

579
00:27:25,339 --> 00:27:27,820
NOT OUT OF TOWN--
GET 'EM OUT OF STATE.

580
00:27:27,820 --> 00:27:29,865
KNOW ANYBODY ON THE EAST COAST?NO.

581
00:27:29,865 --> 00:27:31,911
THAT'S TOO BAD.
HOW ABOUT OVERSEAS?

582
00:27:31,911 --> 00:27:34,609
THAT'S A FIRST-RATE INTERVIEWER
YOU GOT THERE.THANK YOU.

583
00:27:34,609 --> 00:27:36,437
HEY, WHAT'S UP?

584
00:27:36,437 --> 00:27:40,093
SO RIGSBY AND CHO TELL ME THERE
WAS ONLY ONE DUDE WITH A GUN.

585
00:27:40,093 --> 00:27:42,530
THAT DOESN'T SEEM LIKE MUCH.NO, IT'S NOT.

586
00:27:42,530 --> 00:27:44,445
SO WHEN YOU SAY,
"THESE ARE NOT HIPPIES,

587
00:27:44,445 --> 00:27:46,926
THESE ARE SERIOUS, SERIOUS MEN,"

588
00:27:46,926 --> 00:27:49,537
THAT IMPLIES MANY SCARY MEN
WITH LARGE GUNS, RIGHT?

589
00:27:49,537 --> 00:27:51,974
YES.SO WHY JUST ONE?

590
00:27:51,974 --> 00:27:54,803
I DON'T KNOW.
THEY MIGHT BE LOW ON MONEY.

591
00:27:54,803 --> 00:27:57,632
I MEAN,
THE--THE CROP IS DOING BADLY.PLANTS ARE DYING?

592
00:27:57,632 --> 00:28:00,635
YEAH, YEAH. AND THE WORD IS
THAT IT'S BEEN GOING ON

593
00:28:00,635 --> 00:28:03,377
FOR ABOUT SIX MONTHS,
AND NOBODY CAN FIGURE IT OUT,

594
00:28:03,377 --> 00:28:05,771
AND THEY'RE REALLY KIND OF
FREAKING OUT ABOUT IT.I'M SURE.

595
00:28:05,771 --> 00:28:08,164
JANE?YEAH?

596
00:28:08,164 --> 00:28:11,080
UH, I THINK I GOTTA--
I GOTTA GO. I'LL SEE YOU LATER.

597
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:12,342
THANK YOU.

598
00:28:12,342 --> 00:28:14,388
SO WHAT'D YOU GET
FROM THE GUY?

599
00:28:14,388 --> 00:28:16,956
THE POT FARMERS
DIDN'T KILL LEONARD.THAT SO?

600
00:28:16,956 --> 00:28:18,958
YEP.YOU CERTAIN?

601
00:28:18,958 --> 00:28:22,091
WELL, CERTAINTY IS
THE MOTHER OF FOOLS.

602
00:28:22,091 --> 00:28:24,485
SO ALL THIS IS JUST...

603
00:28:24,485 --> 00:28:26,313
GUESSWORK WITH YOU?

604
00:28:26,313 --> 00:28:28,097
PRETTY MUCH.

605
00:28:28,097 --> 00:28:31,622
I MEAN, THAT'S--
THAT'S WHAT I DO, I GUESS.

606
00:28:31,622 --> 00:28:33,755
FOR INSTANCE,
I GUESS THAT YOU'RE MARRIED.

607
00:28:33,755 --> 00:28:35,539
I'M WEARING A RING.

608
00:28:35,539 --> 00:28:38,934
WELL, I GUESS THAT YOU'RE
MARRIED, BUT NOT HAPPILY.

609
00:28:38,934 --> 00:28:42,068
NOT THAT THERE'S
DIVORCE PROCEEDINGS IN PLACE,

610
00:28:42,068 --> 00:28:44,070
BUT...

611
00:28:44,070 --> 00:28:46,507
POSSIBLY A TRIAL SEPARATION.

612
00:28:46,507 --> 00:28:49,118
GUESS I SHOULD'VE
PUT UP A PHOTO, HUH?

613
00:28:49,118 --> 00:28:50,946
MM-HMM.

614
00:28:50,946 --> 00:28:54,036
I KNOW YOU'RE NOT GIVING ME
RELATIONSHIP ADVICE,

615
00:28:54,036 --> 00:28:56,865
SO I HAVE TO WONDER
WHY YOU WOULD GO THERE.

616
00:28:56,865 --> 00:29:00,216
I GUESS IT'S YOUR WAY
OF EXPRESSING UNHAPPINESS.

617
00:29:00,216 --> 00:29:02,305
MM, COULD BE.

618
00:29:02,305 --> 00:29:05,308
I GUESS
IT'S YOUR WAY OF SAYING

619
00:29:05,308 --> 00:29:08,616
YOU'RE UNHAPPY WITH THE WAY
I'M HANDLING LISBON.

620
00:29:08,616 --> 00:29:10,618
WE SPEND
A LOT OF TIME TOGETHER.

621
00:29:10,618 --> 00:29:14,840
AND WHEN SHE'S UNHAPPY,
UH, I'M LESS HAPPY.

622
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:16,363
IT'S HUMAN NATURE.

623
00:29:16,363 --> 00:29:17,973
YES, IT IS.

624
00:29:17,973 --> 00:29:20,019
I'LL TELL YOU WHAT,
PATRICK.

625
00:29:20,019 --> 00:29:23,065
WHY DON'T YOU LET ME
HANDLE MY BUSINESS MY WAY

626
00:29:23,065 --> 00:29:25,546
AND THEN JUDGE ME
BY THE RESULTS?

627
00:29:25,546 --> 00:29:28,070
AND I'LL LET YOU
HANDLE YOURS YOUR WAY...

628
00:29:28,070 --> 00:29:29,463
UP TO A POINT.

629
00:29:29,463 --> 00:29:31,073
THAT SOUNDS FAIR.

630
00:29:31,073 --> 00:29:33,075
UP TO A POINT.

631
00:29:33,075 --> 00:29:35,991
YEAH, VERY FAIR. WE DONE?

632
00:29:35,991 --> 00:29:37,427
NO.

633
00:29:37,427 --> 00:29:39,473
PLEASE DON'T INTERRUPT
INTERROGATIONS.

634
00:29:39,473 --> 00:29:41,780
IT'S RUDE.THAT'S A RULE, IS IT?

635
00:29:41,780 --> 00:29:43,607
GUIDELINE.

636
00:29:43,607 --> 00:29:45,871
I'LL KEEP IT IN MIND.

637
00:29:45,871 --> 00:29:47,394
NOW WE'RE DONE.

638
00:29:49,135 --> 00:29:52,051
LOVING THOSE PUMPS.

639
00:29:52,051 --> 00:29:54,227
THANK YOU.

640
00:29:54,227 --> 00:29:56,490
BYE.

641
00:29:56,490 --> 00:29:58,013
[blinds clatter]

642
00:29:58,013 --> 00:30:00,886
[typing]

643
00:30:04,454 --> 00:30:06,108
OH, WHAT'S THIS?
INTERESTING.

644
00:30:06,108 --> 00:30:07,327
[lowered voice]
WE NEED TO TAKE AMNESIA GIRL

645
00:30:07,327 --> 00:30:10,025
UP TO THE RESERVATION.

646
00:30:10,025 --> 00:30:13,289
MEET ME IN THE PARKING LOT
IN TEN MINUTES.[lowered voice] WHY TAKE HER
TO THE RESERVATION?

647
00:30:13,289 --> 00:30:15,726
THEY'RE HOLDING A MEMORIAL
FOR LEONARD RAILTON.

648
00:30:15,726 --> 00:30:19,034
SHE SHOULD BE THERE.
SHE MIGHT REMEMBER SOMETHING.WORTH A TRY, I GUESS.

649
00:30:19,034 --> 00:30:20,906
OH, DO ME A FAVOR.HMM?

650
00:30:20,906 --> 00:30:23,909
DON'T MENTION THIS
TO LISBON OR HIGHTOWER.AND WHY NOT?

651
00:30:23,909 --> 00:30:26,215
WELL, WHY COMPLICATE THINGS?COMPLICATE HOW?

652
00:30:26,215 --> 00:30:28,870
HELL, VAN PELT,
YOU SHOULDN'T HAVE TAKEN HER

653
00:30:28,870 --> 00:30:31,046
OUT OF THE HOSPITAL
IN THE FIRST PLACE.

654
00:30:31,046 --> 00:30:33,919
YOUR CAR,
PARKING LOT, TEN MINUTES.

655
00:30:33,919 --> 00:30:37,836
[man chanting in
Native American language]

656
00:30:39,620 --> 00:30:42,753
MR. JANE,
WHAT ARE YOU DOING HERE?

657
00:30:42,753 --> 00:30:45,800
WELL, WE'RE HERE
TO PAY OUR RESPECTS.

658
00:30:45,800 --> 00:30:47,715
IT'S OKAY.
WE WON'T EAT MUCH.

659
00:30:47,715 --> 00:30:51,371
LEONARD HAD ONLY BEEN WITH US
A SHORT WHILE,

660
00:30:51,371 --> 00:30:53,721
BUT IF YOU SAW HIM

661
00:30:53,721 --> 00:30:56,898
WALKING A TRAIL UP AT THE LAKES
OR RIDING A HORSE,

662
00:30:56,898 --> 00:30:58,813
YOU COULD SEE

663
00:30:58,813 --> 00:31:00,902
THAT HE WAS HOME.

664
00:31:00,902 --> 00:31:03,470
SO REMEMBER THE OLD WORDS.

665
00:31:03,470 --> 00:31:05,472
WHEN A FRIEND DIES,

666
00:31:05,472 --> 00:31:06,865
WE SHOULD NOT CRY.

667
00:31:06,865 --> 00:31:10,172
WE SHOULD NOT HATE SOMEONE

668
00:31:10,172 --> 00:31:11,782
OR FIGHT.

669
00:31:11,782 --> 00:31:15,917
WE SHOULD DO RIGHT ALWAYS.

670
00:31:15,917 --> 00:31:18,528
AND WE SHOULD LISTEN
TO THE OLD WORDS

671
00:31:18,528 --> 00:31:20,966
AND REMEMBER LEONARD.

672
00:31:20,966 --> 00:31:24,534
IF ANYONE ELSE
HAS SOMETHING TO SAY...

673
00:31:24,534 --> 00:31:25,884
OH, I WOULD.

674
00:31:27,581 --> 00:31:30,149
THIS WOMAN WAS WITH LEONARD
WHEN HE WAS SHOT.

675
00:31:30,149 --> 00:31:32,151
SHE HAS LOST HER MEMORY.

676
00:31:32,151 --> 00:31:35,502
SO WE BROUGHT HER HERE TODAY

677
00:31:35,502 --> 00:31:37,896
TO SEE IF A FACE

678
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:40,115
OR A PLACE OR ANYTHING

679
00:31:40,115 --> 00:31:42,509
COULD HELP HER REMEMBER
WHO SHE IS.

680
00:31:42,509 --> 00:31:46,730
THIS IS KIND OF A SACRED MOMENT.
IS THIS REALLY THE TIME?

681
00:31:46,730 --> 00:31:48,907
IT'LL TAKE BUT A SECOND.

682
00:31:53,346 --> 00:31:54,869
[Patrick] ANYTHING?

683
00:31:54,869 --> 00:31:57,916
NO.

684
00:31:57,916 --> 00:32:01,006
NEVER MIND. THE TRIP
WAS NOT ENTIRELY WASTED.

685
00:32:01,006 --> 00:32:05,271
I WAS ALSO LOOKING AT ALL OF YOU
TO SEE IF ANYONE RECOGNIZED HER.

686
00:32:05,271 --> 00:32:09,492
AND IT SEEMS TO ME THAT SOMEBODY
HERE DOESKNOW THIS WOMAN.

687
00:32:09,492 --> 00:32:12,408
AND THAT SOMEBODY
IS YOU, SIR.

688
00:32:12,408 --> 00:32:14,454
ME?

689
00:32:14,454 --> 00:32:17,065
I THINK YOU'RE MISTAKEN.

690
00:32:17,065 --> 00:32:18,806
PROVE IT.

691
00:32:18,806 --> 00:32:20,677
[grunts] HOW?

692
00:32:22,984 --> 00:32:24,812
LOOK INTO MY EYES

693
00:32:24,812 --> 00:32:26,422
AND HOLD THIS.

694
00:32:30,035 --> 00:32:33,081
NOW TELL ME
YOU DON'T KNOW HER.

695
00:32:33,081 --> 00:32:35,127
I DO NOT KNOW THIS WOMAN.

696
00:32:38,043 --> 00:32:39,958
OKAY.

697
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:41,960
UM, UM, OKAY.

698
00:32:41,960 --> 00:32:44,005
IT APPEARS
THAT I'M MISTAKEN,

699
00:32:44,005 --> 00:32:46,529
WHICH IS VERY GOOD FOR YOU.

700
00:32:46,529 --> 00:32:48,923
THAT ELIMINATES YOU
FROM OUR INQUIRY.

701
00:32:48,923 --> 00:32:50,969
MY APOLOGIES. CARRY ON. WE'LL
JUST TAKE OUR SEATS IN THE BACK.

702
00:32:50,969 --> 00:32:52,709
THANK YOU.

703
00:32:52,709 --> 00:32:56,104
AND, LISTEN, IF YOU--
IF YOU DON'T WANT US HERE,

704
00:32:56,104 --> 00:32:58,280
THEN JUST SAY THE WORD
AND WE'LL GO. JUST SAY THE WORD.

705
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:01,762
[Joseph] I THINK
IT WOULD BE BETTER--I SEE IT.

706
00:33:01,762 --> 00:33:05,157
I SEE IT! I SEE IT! I SEE IT!

707
00:33:05,157 --> 00:33:08,073
I SEE IT.

708
00:33:08,073 --> 00:33:12,077
[laughing]

709
00:33:15,515 --> 00:33:19,475
NOW JUST RELAX, BREATHE
AND TELL US WHAT YOU SEE.

710
00:33:19,475 --> 00:33:22,478
THERE'S A BLUE LAKE...

711
00:33:22,478 --> 00:33:25,090
PINE TREES...

712
00:33:25,090 --> 00:33:27,135
A MOUNTAIN...

713
00:33:27,135 --> 00:33:28,832
THERE'S A BIRD SINGING.

714
00:33:32,271 --> 00:33:35,143
TELL US WHAT'S HAPPENING
AT THIS LAKE.

715
00:33:35,143 --> 00:33:37,493
IT'S WHERE
THE BAD THING HAPPENED.

716
00:33:37,493 --> 00:33:40,714
WHAT BAD THING?

717
00:33:40,714 --> 00:33:42,759
GO LOOK. THEY...

718
00:33:42,759 --> 00:33:45,501
THEY LEFT SOMETHING
ON THE SHORE.

719
00:33:45,501 --> 00:33:48,113
WHO DID?GO LOOK.
THEY LEFT SOMETHING.

720
00:33:48,113 --> 00:33:50,289
[whispers]
THEY LEFT SOMETHING.

721
00:33:55,076 --> 00:33:57,078
I'M SORRY.

722
00:33:57,078 --> 00:33:59,863
OKAY, SHOW'S OVER. COME ON.

723
00:33:59,863 --> 00:34:01,909
WATCH YOUR HEAD.

724
00:34:01,909 --> 00:34:04,477
SO MR. SILVERWING IS
GONNA COMPLAIN TO OUR SUPERIORS

725
00:34:04,477 --> 00:34:06,522
IN THE STRONGEST TERMS.
NICE WORK.

726
00:34:06,522 --> 00:34:09,960
SEE, THAT'S WHY I DIDN'T BRING
YOU ALONG--DENIABILITY.

727
00:34:09,960 --> 00:34:13,834
HOW DID YOU KNOW WE WERE HERE?I HAD LITTLE, TINY
G.P.S. TRACKERS

728
00:34:13,834 --> 00:34:15,836
SEWN INTO ALL YOUR SUITS.

729
00:34:15,836 --> 00:34:19,840
FOR A SECOND THERE, I ALMOST
BELIEVED YOU. GRACE?

730
00:34:19,840 --> 00:34:23,539
SORRY, JANE.
I HAD TO TELL HER. IT'S MY JOB.EH, THAT'S NOT IT.

731
00:34:23,539 --> 00:34:26,238
GET HER BACK TO THE HOSPITAL.YES, BOSS.

732
00:34:26,238 --> 00:34:28,153
SHE DIDREMEMBER SOMETHING.
WE HAVE A CLUE.

733
00:34:28,153 --> 00:34:31,025
A LAKE IN THE MOUNTAIN,
SOMETHING ON THE SHORE?

734
00:34:31,025 --> 00:34:34,289
COULD BE WHERE
THE MURDERS HAPPENED.THERE'S OVER 50 LAKES
IN THOSE MOUNTAINS!

735
00:34:34,289 --> 00:34:38,250
I'LL TAKE HER BACK
TO THE HOSPITAL.LISTEN, I'M SORRY I DIDN'T
TELL YOU WHERE I WAS GOING.

736
00:34:38,250 --> 00:34:40,078
I WASTRYING
TO PROTECT YOU.

737
00:34:40,078 --> 00:34:42,384
I KNEW I WAS
GONNA STIR THINGS UP,

738
00:34:42,384 --> 00:34:46,084
AND, WHAT, WITH HIGHTOWER ALL-- DON'T.DON'T EVER TRY
TO PROTECT ME.

739
00:34:46,084 --> 00:34:48,825
I CAN PROTECT MYSELF
FROM HIGHTOWER OR ANYBODY ELSE.OKAY.

740
00:34:48,825 --> 00:34:52,264
LET'S GO BACK
TO THE OFFICE.WE COULD.
OR WE COULD STAY HERE

741
00:34:52,264 --> 00:34:55,441
AND CATCH
LEONARD RAILTON'S KILLER.HOW ARE WE GONNA DO THAT?

742
00:34:55,441 --> 00:34:57,486
I NEED A CUP.

743
00:34:57,486 --> 00:35:00,054
PAPER OR PLASTIC--
I'D PREFER PAPER.[car door opens]

744
00:35:02,535 --> 00:35:06,016
[car door slams]SO JANE DOE
DIDN'T REMEMBER THE LAKE?

745
00:35:06,016 --> 00:35:07,714
POSTHYPNOTIC SUGGESTION.

746
00:35:07,714 --> 00:35:10,412
I SHOWED HER A BEAUTIFUL PICTURE
OF A LAKE AND TOLD HER

747
00:35:10,412 --> 00:35:12,980
THAT SHE WOULD REMEMBER IT WHEN
SHE HEARD THE TRIGGER PHRASE--

748
00:35:12,980 --> 00:35:15,591
"SAY THE WORD." SHE REMEMBERED
THE PICTURE, ASSOCIATED IT

749
00:35:15,591 --> 00:35:18,855
WITH THE CRIME AND FELT THAT
SOMETHING WAS LEFT BEHIND THERE.WHAT SOMETHING?

750
00:35:18,855 --> 00:35:20,466
WELL, IT--IT DOESN'T MATTER.

751
00:35:20,466 --> 00:35:23,208
THE KILLER'S FEELING
PARANOID NOW, SO HE OR SHE

752
00:35:23,208 --> 00:35:26,254
WILL BE COMPELLED TO GO BACK
TO THE SCENE OF THE CRIME

753
00:35:26,254 --> 00:35:30,606
AND MAKE SURE THAT
NOTHING WAS LEFT BEHIND.THAT'S ASSUMING THE MURDER
OCCURRED AT THE LAKE.

754
00:35:30,606 --> 00:35:33,261
WELL, IT DID.BECAUSE?

755
00:35:33,261 --> 00:35:35,829
BECAUSETHE POT CROP DIED,
AND LEONARD RAILTON WAS WORRIED

756
00:35:35,829 --> 00:35:37,831
ABOUT THE WATER HIS
GIRLFRIEND'S BABY WAS GETTING.

757
00:35:37,831 --> 00:35:40,877
HEY, IT'S OVER HERE.AND THE WATER SUPPLY
FOR AROUND HERE

758
00:35:40,877 --> 00:35:43,010
COMES FROM THE MOUNTAIN LAKES.

759
00:35:43,010 --> 00:35:45,186
CHO FOLLOWED THE KILLER
AFTER THE MEMORIAL.

760
00:35:45,186 --> 00:35:47,536
AND? WHO IS IT?WE'LL SEE.

761
00:35:49,973 --> 00:35:51,975
WHERE IS HE?

762
00:35:51,975 --> 00:35:54,152
[Cho]
STRAIGHT THROUGH THE TREES.

763
00:35:57,067 --> 00:35:59,157
[tapping][Cho] HANDS UP.

764
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:01,550
WHAT'S GOING ON?GET YOUR HANDS UP.

765
00:36:01,550 --> 00:36:04,162
NO, I-I DON'T UNDERSTAND.

766
00:36:05,946 --> 00:36:08,296
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

767
00:36:09,906 --> 00:36:11,299
RIFLE SHELL.

768
00:36:11,299 --> 00:36:13,258
WHERE'D YOU GET THAT,
MR. WILLIS?

769
00:36:13,258 --> 00:36:15,129
I JUST FOUND IT.

770
00:36:15,129 --> 00:36:17,131
I WAS GONNA GIVE IT TO YOU.

771
00:36:17,131 --> 00:36:20,134
DO YOU THINK
IT'S CONNECTED TO THOSE MURDERS?[laughing]

772
00:36:20,134 --> 00:36:23,093
THAT'S THE BEST YOU GOT?WHY'D YOU SHOOT
THOSE FOUR PEOPLE, MR. WILLIS?

773
00:36:23,093 --> 00:36:26,096
I DIDN'T.WELL, KEEP IN MIND
THAT TWO OF THEM--

774
00:36:26,096 --> 00:36:29,056
THE LANGHAMS--THEY WERE,
UH, BY-PRODUCTS, LATECOMERS.

775
00:36:29,056 --> 00:36:32,320
BUT LEONARD...

776
00:36:32,320 --> 00:36:35,497
LEONARD YOU KILLED BECAUSE OF
WHAT'S IN THE LAKE, DIDN'T YOU?

777
00:36:35,497 --> 00:36:38,239
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

778
00:36:38,239 --> 00:36:40,328
TOXIC WASTE.

779
00:36:40,328 --> 00:36:42,504
GREAT, BIG BARRELS OF IT,
I EXPECT.

780
00:36:42,504 --> 00:36:44,114
DUMPED BY YOU.

781
00:36:44,114 --> 00:36:47,292
THAT'S WHY THE POT PLANTS
IN THE VALLEY WERE DYING.

782
00:36:47,292 --> 00:36:49,816
THAT'S WHY DERRIEN HOPWOOD'S
CHILD GOT A RASH.

783
00:36:49,816 --> 00:36:52,035
LEONARD WAS GONNA TELL,

784
00:36:52,035 --> 00:36:54,473
SO YOU HAD TO SHOOT HIM.

785
00:36:54,473 --> 00:36:58,128
AND ANYONE ELSE THAT JUST...
HAPPENED TO COME ALONG THAT DAY.

786
00:36:58,128 --> 00:37:00,305
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
WHAT TO SAY.

787
00:37:00,305 --> 00:37:02,785
THAT IS NOTTRUE.

788
00:37:02,785 --> 00:37:05,571
WELL, THIS IS GROUND ZERO
FOR THE DUMPING,

789
00:37:05,571 --> 00:37:08,487
SO THE WATER HERE MUST BE
MUCH MORE TOXIC

790
00:37:08,487 --> 00:37:11,011
THAN IT IS DOWN IN THE VALLEY.THAT IS NONSENSE!

791
00:37:11,011 --> 00:37:12,621
[Patrick] REALLY?

792
00:37:12,621 --> 00:37:15,189
FEELING A LITTLE PARCHED?
HAVE A DRINK.

793
00:37:15,189 --> 00:37:16,582
NO.

794
00:37:16,582 --> 00:37:19,541
NO.WHY NOT?

795
00:37:19,541 --> 00:37:22,196
OH, COME ON.
CHEERS. HAVE A DRINK.NO.

796
00:37:22,196 --> 00:37:24,154
LITTLE SIP.NO. NO, PLEASE, STOP.
NO!

797
00:37:24,154 --> 00:37:25,852
[grunts] ALL RIGHT!

798
00:37:25,852 --> 00:37:29,812
I TRIED TO GET SO MANY IDEAS
ACROSS THE TRIBAL COUNCIL.

799
00:37:29,812 --> 00:37:33,207
[sighs]
BUT SOMEBODY DIDN'T LIKE IT,

800
00:37:33,207 --> 00:37:35,253
OR IT WASN'T
CULTURALLY APPROPRIATE,

801
00:37:35,253 --> 00:37:37,820
OR BLAH, DE, BLAH, DE, BLAH.

802
00:37:37,820 --> 00:37:40,301
SO THIS GUY SAID

803
00:37:40,301 --> 00:37:42,216
HE NEEDED TO DUMP
SOME STUFF,

804
00:37:42,216 --> 00:37:46,873
AND DID I KNOW ANY PLACE
ON THE REZ THAT HE COULD DO IT?

805
00:37:46,873 --> 00:37:49,876
SO I HAD LEONARD TAKE THEM
UP TO THE LAKE.

806
00:37:49,876 --> 00:37:52,400
WELL, I FIGURED WITH HIS RECORD,
HE'D TAKE THE MONEY

807
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:55,577
AND KEEP HIS MOUTH SHUT.

808
00:37:55,577 --> 00:37:57,231
WELL, WE WENT WELL.

809
00:37:58,798 --> 00:38:00,930
[thud] GOT MORE TRUCKS UP THERE.

810
00:38:00,930 --> 00:38:03,368
I MEAN, SOMETHING WAS
FINALLY WORKING FOR ME.

811
00:38:05,326 --> 00:38:08,286
AND THEN THAT KID IN THE VALLEY
GOT A RASH.

812
00:38:08,286 --> 00:38:10,331
AND LEONARD WAS WORRIED.

813
00:38:10,331 --> 00:38:12,638
SAID WEWERE
POISONING THE VALLEY,

814
00:38:12,638 --> 00:38:17,338
AND IF WE DIDN'T STOP, THAT
HE WAS GONNA BLOW THE WHISTLE.

815
00:38:17,338 --> 00:38:21,168
THEN I OVERHEARD HIM
ON THE PHONE,

816
00:38:21,168 --> 00:38:24,040
ARRANGING TO MEET SOMEBODY
UP AT THE LAKE.

817
00:38:26,216 --> 00:38:28,436
SO I WENT, TOO.

818
00:38:32,919 --> 00:38:34,834
[gunshot]

819
00:38:37,097 --> 00:38:39,055
[gunshot]

820
00:38:39,055 --> 00:38:41,101
WHEN DID THE LANGHAMS
GET THERE?

821
00:38:41,101 --> 00:38:42,972
I WAS CLEANING UP.

822
00:38:46,889 --> 00:38:49,022
YOU KNOW,
WHAT THEY DOING THERE, ANYWAY?

823
00:38:49,022 --> 00:38:50,806
[gunshot]

824
00:38:50,806 --> 00:38:52,199
[gunshot]

825
00:38:52,199 --> 00:38:55,158
UM,
THEY WERE TAKING A HIKE?

826
00:38:55,158 --> 00:38:57,073
[sighs]

827
00:39:00,163 --> 00:39:03,384
[voice breaking] I'M SORRY.

828
00:39:03,384 --> 00:39:06,169
I AM.

829
00:39:06,169 --> 00:39:07,606
[whispers] I'M SORRY.

830
00:39:09,956 --> 00:39:11,958
WELL, THAT'S OKAY, THEN.

831
00:39:11,958 --> 00:39:15,527
AS LONG AS YOU'RE SORRY.
MAYBE WE'LL JUST LET YOU GO.

832
00:39:21,010 --> 00:39:22,969
I'M KIDDING.

833
00:39:24,971 --> 00:39:26,799
[knock on window]

834
00:39:30,063 --> 00:39:33,153
HEY.
GOT SOMETHING FOR YOU.

835
00:39:33,153 --> 00:39:35,155
YOUR DRIVER'S LICENSE.

836
00:39:35,155 --> 00:39:37,505
WE GOT IT
FROM MARKHAM WILLIS.

837
00:39:39,246 --> 00:39:42,728
YOUR NAME IS CAMILLE DILLON.
YOU LIVE IN OAKLAND.

838
00:39:42,728 --> 00:39:45,252
YOU'RE AN INTERNET JOURNALIST
AND WRITER.

839
00:39:45,252 --> 00:39:47,254
WE CONTACTED YOUR FAMILY.

840
00:39:47,254 --> 00:39:49,691
YOUR MOM IS ON HER WAY
FROM DES MOINES.

841
00:39:51,476 --> 00:39:53,826
MY NAME IS CAMILLE?

842
00:39:53,826 --> 00:39:55,828
APPARENTLY,
YOU TAUGHT LEONARD RAILTON

843
00:39:55,828 --> 00:39:58,047
WHILE HE WAS
IN THE JUVENILE SYSTEM.

844
00:39:58,047 --> 00:40:01,181
A LITTLE WHILE AGO,
HE GOT IN TOUCH WITH YOU ABOUT--

845
00:40:01,181 --> 00:40:02,748
WAIT.

846
00:40:02,748 --> 00:40:06,665
SOMETHING...
SOMETHING WAS WRONG.

847
00:40:06,665 --> 00:40:08,928
THEY WERE...

848
00:40:08,928 --> 00:40:12,061
SOMEONE WAS, UH, DUMPING...

849
00:40:12,061 --> 00:40:14,499
TOXINS.Y-YES.

850
00:40:14,499 --> 00:40:19,025
AND HE--
HE WANTED PEOPLE TO KNOW. HE...

851
00:40:19,025 --> 00:40:21,070
HE CALLED...

852
00:40:21,070 --> 00:40:23,682
AND HE--HE ASKED
FOR MY HELP.

853
00:40:23,682 --> 00:40:25,466
I REM--

854
00:40:25,466 --> 00:40:26,989
I REMEMBER HIM.

855
00:40:29,688 --> 00:40:32,691
I REMEMBER HIM
ASKING FOR MY HELP.

856
00:40:32,691 --> 00:40:34,214
[sniffles and whispers]
I REMEMBER.

857
00:40:36,085 --> 00:40:38,523
I REMEMBER ME.

858
00:40:38,523 --> 00:40:42,614
[voice breaking]
I KNOW WHO I AM.

859
00:40:51,666 --> 00:40:53,886
HEY. JUST LET ME
FINISH THIS UP,

860
00:40:53,886 --> 00:40:56,671
AND WE'LL GO
TALK TO HIGHTOWER.

861
00:40:56,671 --> 00:40:58,151
WAYNE...

862
00:40:58,151 --> 00:40:59,979
WHAT'S UP?

863
00:41:02,068 --> 00:41:06,028
I LOVE YOU. I DO.

864
00:41:06,028 --> 00:41:09,031
BUT I THINK
I LOVE THE JOB MORE.

865
00:41:09,031 --> 00:41:11,991
WELL, JOB'S NOT A PROBLEM.
I'M GONNA GO.

866
00:41:11,991 --> 00:41:14,907
YOU'D BE LEAVING THE UNIT...
FOR US.

867
00:41:14,907 --> 00:41:16,909
SO?

868
00:41:16,909 --> 00:41:19,651
I DON'T WANT
THAT RESPONSIBILITY.

869
00:41:19,651 --> 00:41:21,827
YOU'LL HATE ME FOR IT.

870
00:41:21,827 --> 00:41:24,873
[voice breaking] MAYBE NOT
TODAY, BUT SOMEDAY YOU WILL.NO, GRACE, WE--WE--

871
00:41:24,873 --> 00:41:26,745
[whispers] I'M SORRY.

872
00:41:32,011 --> 00:41:34,013
YOU'RE, UH...

873
00:41:34,013 --> 00:41:36,058
CERTAIN ABOUT THIS?

874
00:41:36,058 --> 00:41:40,541
I KNOW WHO I AM.

875
00:41:42,238 --> 00:41:44,719
[chair rolls]

876
00:41:51,944 --> 00:41:53,772
NARCOTICS PICKED UP
THE POT FARMERS

877
00:41:53,772 --> 00:41:55,338
OFF THE RANGER'S CONFESSION.

878
00:41:55,338 --> 00:41:58,603
I ALSO GOT A CALL
FROM A GUY NAMED SILVERWING

879
00:41:58,603 --> 00:42:02,563
ABOUT A STUNT YOU PULLED UP ON
THE STORM RIVER RESERVATION.WELL, I WOULDN'T CALL THAT
A STUNT SO M--

880
00:42:02,563 --> 00:42:05,566
WHATEVER. HE WAS DISPLEASED.YES, MA'AM.
I FILLED OUT A P-90--

881
00:42:05,566 --> 00:42:07,742
YOU SOLVED THE TRIPLE,
RIGHT?YEAH.

882
00:42:07,742 --> 00:42:09,788
NOBODY GOT HURT?[Patrick] NO.

883
00:42:09,788 --> 00:42:12,399
THEN THE HELL WITH HIM.
YOU GOT JUSTICE DONE.

884
00:42:12,399 --> 00:42:14,619
KEEP UP THE GOOD WORK.

885
00:42:19,493 --> 00:42:21,495
THAT WAS UNEXPECTED.

886
00:42:21,495 --> 00:42:23,410
I'LL SAY.

887
00:42:27,675 --> 00:42:29,068
HEY, GRACE.

888
00:42:29,068 --> 00:42:31,505
HI. [sniffles][elevator bell dings]

889
00:42:31,505 --> 00:42:33,333
YOU ALL RIGHT?[crying] I'M FINE.

890
00:42:33,333 --> 00:42:35,422
OKAY, BUT...[sobbing]

891
00:42:35,422 --> 00:42:36,945
YEAH, I-I JUST...

892
00:42:40,383 --> 00:42:43,561
I JUST, UH, FORGOT MY... STUFF.

893
00:42:43,561 --> 00:42:46,476
[continues sobbing]

894
00:42:51,220 --> 00:42:54,006
STAY TUNED FOR SCENES
FROM OUR NEXT EPISODE.

